From 1cb04299d177671ea3cb0273dff5b0708a4713d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:21:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bsps/ofw: Do not write into a const buffer in
 rtems_ofw_node_status()

rtems_ofw_node_status() declared its scratch buffer const, then cast the
const away to let rtems_ofw_get_prop() fill it in:

  const char buf[10];

  len = rtems_ofw_get_prop(node, "status", (void *)&buf[0], sizeof(buf));

Modifying an object defined with a const-qualified type is undefined
behaviour.  A compiler is entitled to assume buf never changes after its
(absent) initialisation and to fold the subsequent strncmp() calls
against indeterminate contents, in which case a node's "status" property
is never really examined and rtems_ofw_node_status() returns an answer
unrelated to the device tree.

clang reports this as

  error: default initialization of an object of type 'const char[10]'
  leaves the object uninitialized [-Wdefault-const-init-var-unsafe]

Drop the const, which also removes the need for the cast.  There is no
reason for the buffer to be const: it is a local output buffer.

rtems_ofw_get_prop() already takes a void * rather than a const void *,
so no other change is needed.

ofw01, fdt01 and fdt02 pass on riscv/mbv before and after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bsps/shared/ofw/ofw.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bsps/shared/ofw/ofw.c b/bsps/shared/ofw/ofw.c
index 5567df75f3..97af8bf23f 100644
--- a/bsps/shared/ofw/ofw.c
+++ b/bsps/shared/ofw/ofw.c
@@ -684,9 +684,9 @@ int rtems_ofw_get_interrupts(
 bool rtems_ofw_node_status( phandle_t node )
 {
   int len;
-  const char buf[10];
+  char buf[10];
 
-  len = rtems_ofw_get_prop(node, "status", (void *)&buf[0], sizeof(buf));
+  len = rtems_ofw_get_prop(node, "status", &buf[0], sizeof(buf));
   if ((len == -1) ||
       (strncmp(buf, "okay", MIN(5, len)) == 0) ||
       (strncmp(buf, "ok", MIN(3, len)) == 0)) {
-- 
